1
00:00:11,268 --> 00:00:17,691
[FRIDA humming]

2
00:00:25,157 --> 00:00:31,121
[FRIDA humming]

3
00:00:45,051 --> 00:00:47,471
[gasps]

4
00:02:34,119 --> 00:02:37,873
Before we go on, are there
any questions up to this point?

5
00:02:37,915 --> 00:02:41,919
Hm? Appears Lucian's
absent again today.

6
00:02:41,961 --> 00:02:42,544
Has anyone seen him?

7
00:02:42,586 --> 00:02:44,880
[TATE gasps]
Professor!

8
00:02:44,922 --> 00:02:46,673
Yes? What is it, Tate?

9
00:02:46,715 --> 00:02:49,718
[TATE]
Lucian's-- Well, you see, uh...

10
00:02:49,760 --> 00:02:50,970
He has a cold.

11
00:02:51,011 --> 00:02:53,472
A cold? I'm sorry to hear.

12
00:02:53,513 --> 00:02:56,433
Right. After the lecture,
I think I'll pay him a visit.

13
00:02:56,475 --> 00:02:58,310
No! You don't have to do that!

14
00:02:58,351 --> 00:03:01,229
You see, Lucian and I share
the same dormitory room,

15
00:03:01,271 --> 00:03:04,357
so I'm looking after him.

16
00:03:04,399 --> 00:03:08,821
Interesting. Well,
that's a relief to hear.

17
00:03:10,948 --> 00:03:13,784
[CLERK 05A]
Tate Percival and Lucian Atwood?

18
00:03:13,826 --> 00:03:17,329
I'll find the information
for you right away, sir.

19
00:03:31,760 --> 00:03:35,055
[WILLIAM] Lucian is the heir
to the Atwood viscountcy.

20
00:03:35,097 --> 00:03:37,891
A lineage that goes
back over two centuries.

21
00:03:37,933 --> 00:03:40,602
Similar to Tate's.

22
00:03:40,644 --> 00:03:44,064
So both of them are heirs
to aristocratic families.

23
00:03:50,236 --> 00:03:52,698
[TATE] I can't cover
for you much longer.

24
00:03:52,739 --> 00:03:54,950
Honestly, where'd
you disappear to?

25
00:03:54,992 --> 00:03:58,495
[sneezes]

26
00:03:58,537 --> 00:04:01,081
On top of everything,
now I've got a cold.

27
00:04:01,123 --> 00:04:03,125
[knocking]

28
00:04:04,751 --> 00:04:05,794
[TATE]
Yes?

29
00:04:05,836 --> 00:04:09,297
[gasps] Professor Moriarty!
Why're you here?

30
00:04:09,339 --> 00:04:11,925
That was an
impressive sneeze, Tate.

31
00:04:11,967 --> 00:04:15,012
I heard it clearly
through the door.

32
00:04:15,054 --> 00:04:17,806
Then again, you've been
looking after Lucian.

33
00:04:17,848 --> 00:04:19,766
Perhaps you caught his cold?

34
00:04:19,808 --> 00:04:21,101
Uhh...

35
00:04:21,143 --> 00:04:23,854
[TATE stammers]
Th-That's probably it.

36
00:04:23,896 --> 00:04:25,064
Professor!

37
00:04:25,105 --> 00:04:26,982
Wait. I wouldn't--

38
00:04:27,024 --> 00:04:29,442
There's no need for that!

39
00:04:29,484 --> 00:04:30,736
[TATE gasps]

40
00:04:30,777 --> 00:04:32,905
[WILLIAM] This bed hasn't
been slept in for some time.

41
00:04:32,946 --> 00:04:34,406
[TATE]
Well...

42
00:04:35,490 --> 00:04:38,118
I suggest you start
talking, and quickly.

43
00:04:38,160 --> 00:04:39,285
[TATE yelps]

44
00:04:41,163 --> 00:04:42,581
Despite my demeanor,

45
00:04:42,622 --> 00:04:46,376
at this moment, I'm more cross
than you could possibly imagine.

46
00:04:46,418 --> 00:04:49,046
[whimpers]

47
00:04:50,589 --> 00:04:52,549
[TATE sighs]

48
00:04:52,591 --> 00:04:53,759
Do you mean to tell me that

49
00:04:53,800 --> 00:04:56,553
Lucian hasn't been to the
dormitory in three days?

50
00:04:56,595 --> 00:04:57,846
Sneaking out of the dorms and

51
00:04:57,888 --> 00:05:00,265
being gone all night
isn't anything new.

52
00:05:00,306 --> 00:05:02,475
But he's always back
the next morning.

53
00:05:02,517 --> 00:05:04,895
He should've returned by now.

54
00:05:04,937 --> 00:05:08,356
I was worried, so I went
down to check at the pub.

55
00:05:08,398 --> 00:05:10,316
There's a waitress
there named Frida

56
00:05:10,358 --> 00:05:13,779
who Lucian is
absolutely mad about.

57
00:05:13,820 --> 00:05:16,240
If he was spending
the night anywhere,

58
00:05:16,281 --> 00:05:20,577
I would've expected it
to be at her place.

59
00:05:20,619 --> 00:05:22,913
- -[TATE gasps]
- -[HOSTESS 05A] Piss off!

60
00:05:25,624 --> 00:05:29,169
[WILLIAM] That explains it--
at least how you got your cold.

61
00:05:29,211 --> 00:05:32,798
However, such a harsh welcome
and without warning is odd.

62
00:05:32,839 --> 00:05:33,882
Leads me to believe

63
00:05:33,924 --> 00:05:36,384
there may have been
some trouble beforehand.

64
00:05:38,678 --> 00:05:42,474
[TATE] Look, Professor,
he may be a foolhardy gadabout,

65
00:05:42,515 --> 00:05:44,893
but he has a good heart.

66
00:05:44,935 --> 00:05:46,478
I'll say this,

67
00:05:46,519 --> 00:05:50,356
it doesn't matter what
he's got himself mixed up in,

68
00:05:50,398 --> 00:05:54,027
I just want to bring him home.

69
00:05:54,069 --> 00:05:56,155
It sounds to me like
you're very concerned

70
00:05:56,196 --> 00:05:57,906
about Lucian's wellbeing.

71
00:05:57,948 --> 00:06:00,075
Of course, I am, sir!

72
00:06:00,117 --> 00:06:01,743
Why say "of course"?

73
00:06:01,785 --> 00:06:05,038
[TATE]
I mean, because...

74
00:06:05,080 --> 00:06:07,373
...Lucian is my friend!

75
00:06:12,963 --> 00:06:14,089
[WILLIAM]
From here on,

76
00:06:14,131 --> 00:06:17,383
I think it's best if you
stay out of the matter.

77
00:06:17,425 --> 00:06:20,345
Leave this to me;
I'll deal with Lucian.

78
00:06:20,386 --> 00:06:22,472
Uh, yes, sir.

79
00:06:23,515 --> 00:06:24,349
[WILLIAM]
And Tate...

80
00:06:24,390 --> 00:06:25,600
[TATE]
Hm?

81
00:06:27,811 --> 00:06:31,648
No fortune's greater than the
bond shared between friends.

82
00:06:39,781 --> 00:06:42,408
[DUDLEY]
Professor Moriarty, I presume?

83
00:06:42,450 --> 00:06:43,743
[WILLIAM]
And you are?

84
00:06:43,785 --> 00:06:45,037
The name's Dudley Bale,

85
00:06:45,078 --> 00:06:48,581
a humble administrative
assistant for the university.

86
00:06:48,623 --> 00:06:50,042
I've seen you from time-to-time

87
00:06:50,083 --> 00:06:52,169
strolling about
the campus grounds.

88
00:06:52,211 --> 00:06:54,254
Please, forgive my manners.

89
00:06:54,296 --> 00:06:56,631
Introductions are past due.

90
00:06:56,673 --> 00:06:59,009
I noticed you coming
from the dormitories.

91
00:06:59,051 --> 00:07:01,553
Is something amiss
with one of your students?

92
00:07:01,594 --> 00:07:04,973
[WILLIAM] Possibly. I went
to pay Lucian Atwood a visit.

93
00:07:05,015 --> 00:07:07,642
He's been absent from my
lectures for several days,

94
00:07:07,684 --> 00:07:09,936
so I wanted to check up on him.

95
00:07:09,978 --> 00:07:12,522
Did you catch the
rogue nursing a hangover?

96
00:07:12,564 --> 00:07:14,816
The issue is
finding him actually.

97
00:07:14,858 --> 00:07:16,526
According to his roommate,

98
00:07:16,568 --> 00:07:19,029
he hasn't shown his
face for three days.

99
00:07:19,071 --> 00:07:21,698
Staying out overnight
without permission?

100
00:07:21,740 --> 00:07:25,077
Not uncommon for these boys,
but rules are rules.

101
00:07:25,118 --> 00:07:28,830
Then again, why don't we look
the other way this one time?

102
00:07:28,872 --> 00:07:30,999
Don't want to
come down too hard.

103
00:07:31,041 --> 00:07:34,211
Otherwise, we're bound
to start a rebellion.

104
00:07:34,253 --> 00:07:35,420
But still,

105
00:07:35,461 --> 00:07:38,882
we can agree that three days
is slightly irregular.

106
00:07:38,924 --> 00:07:40,717
Perhaps we should
notify the police.

107
00:07:40,759 --> 00:07:42,427
Normally, I would agree,

108
00:07:42,468 --> 00:07:45,555
but this could be
a very delicate situation.

109
00:07:45,597 --> 00:07:47,974
See, Lucian is
the son of nobility,

110
00:07:48,016 --> 00:07:48,975
and any brush with the law

111
00:07:49,017 --> 00:07:51,853
would reflect poorly on
the family name.

112
00:07:51,895 --> 00:07:54,356
[WILLIAM] Then what?
You'd have us drop the matter?

113
00:07:54,398 --> 00:07:56,316
Don't misunderstand me.

114
00:07:56,358 --> 00:07:57,984
I have connections
with the local police

115
00:07:58,026 --> 00:08:01,321
and could ask them to look into
his disappearance discreetly.

116
00:08:01,363 --> 00:08:03,282
Please, allow me to handle this

117
00:08:03,323 --> 00:08:06,201
to avoid damaging
the family's name.

118
00:08:06,243 --> 00:08:07,744
So, that settles it?

119
00:08:07,786 --> 00:08:10,205
There's no need to be concerned.

120
00:08:11,539 --> 00:08:12,457
[WILLIAM]
This is the pub where

121
00:08:12,498 --> 00:08:15,127
Tate received his
not-so-warm welcome.

122
00:08:15,168 --> 00:08:16,795
[door opens]

123
00:08:19,672 --> 00:08:21,633
We're closed. Come back later.

124
00:08:21,674 --> 00:08:24,177
[WILLIAM]
I realize it's early.

125
00:08:24,219 --> 00:08:26,846
However, I'm not
here to buy a drink.

126
00:08:26,888 --> 00:08:28,556
I'd like to have
a word with you.

127
00:08:28,598 --> 00:08:29,766
[HOSTESS 05A]
Hmm.

128
00:08:31,726 --> 00:08:34,229
[HOSTESS 05A] Just for
talkin' about a dead girl?

129
00:08:34,271 --> 00:08:36,273
This is quite the tip.

130
00:08:36,315 --> 00:08:38,775
You a newspaper
reporter or what?

131
00:08:38,817 --> 00:08:40,235
Nothing like that.

132
00:08:40,277 --> 00:08:42,612
My name's William James Moriarty

133
00:08:42,654 --> 00:08:45,573
and I teach at
Dunham University.

134
00:08:45,615 --> 00:08:47,451
You're a college professor?

135
00:08:47,492 --> 00:08:49,661
If there's an issue
with a student's conduct,

136
00:08:49,702 --> 00:08:53,373
it's my duty as an educator
to set things right.

137
00:08:53,415 --> 00:08:55,167
In order to do that, first,

138
00:08:55,208 --> 00:08:59,129
I must collect all the necessary
facts pertaining to the matter.

139
00:08:59,171 --> 00:09:00,797
[HOSTESS 05A]
Mm.

140
00:09:01,965 --> 00:09:06,052
[HOSTESS 05A] What can I say?
Frida was a wonderful girl.

141
00:09:06,094 --> 00:09:07,804
She loved dancing.

142
00:09:07,846 --> 00:09:12,434
And when she smiled,
the entire room would light up.

143
00:09:12,476 --> 00:09:15,395
A real flower, that one.

144
00:09:15,437 --> 00:09:18,273
Which makes what happened
all the more tragic.

145
00:09:20,566 --> 00:09:23,069
According to the old man
who lived under the bridge,

146
00:09:23,111 --> 00:09:24,529
last thing she was doing was

147
00:09:24,570 --> 00:09:27,949
singin' and dancin' before
she fell into the river.

148
00:09:27,991 --> 00:09:31,995
I wonder what she
was singin' about.

149
00:09:36,166 --> 00:09:37,501
See, Professor,

150
00:09:37,542 --> 00:09:41,754
Frida and this missing student
of yours had fallen in love.

151
00:09:41,796 --> 00:09:44,674
Thing is, he's a
big-shot aristocrat.

152
00:09:44,716 --> 00:09:47,177
Not the same class as us.

153
00:09:47,219 --> 00:09:48,470
I'm sure she thought

154
00:09:48,512 --> 00:09:52,391
he was just looking for
a good time at the beginning.

155
00:09:52,432 --> 00:09:56,228
But then, he proposed
marriage to her.

156
00:09:56,269 --> 00:09:57,645
[FRIDA gasps]

157
00:09:57,687 --> 00:10:02,401
I want to spend the rest of my
days dancing with one person.

158
00:10:02,442 --> 00:10:04,236
You, Frida.

159
00:10:04,277 --> 00:10:06,988
Would you mind being
my dance partner

160
00:10:07,030 --> 00:10:08,823
forever?

161
00:10:08,865 --> 00:10:11,284
[FRIDA giggles]

162
00:10:12,911 --> 00:10:15,080
Not one bit.

163
00:10:16,456 --> 00:10:20,043
[HOSTESS 05A] I tried to talk
her out of it... at first.

164
00:10:20,085 --> 00:10:23,755
Then she told me that
she was with child.

165
00:10:23,796 --> 00:10:27,050
And after seeing that blissful
expression on her face,

166
00:10:27,092 --> 00:10:30,262
I couldn't raise any objections.

167
00:10:30,303 --> 00:10:35,016
However, before long,
he entered the picture.

168
00:10:35,058 --> 00:10:39,896
I don't know exactly what
he said to Frida that night.

169
00:10:39,938 --> 00:10:41,189
But...

170
00:10:43,483 --> 00:10:45,735
[HOSTESS 05A]
...it was at that moment I knew.

171
00:10:45,777 --> 00:10:48,238
She'd been abandoned.

172
00:10:48,280 --> 00:10:51,283
Even so, she
gathered herself up,

173
00:10:51,324 --> 00:10:54,702
said she would raise
the child by herself.

174
00:10:54,744 --> 00:10:57,122
And then...

175
00:10:57,163 --> 00:10:59,707
I just asked you to
recount a harrowing tale.

176
00:10:59,749 --> 00:11:01,626
Please forgive me.

177
00:11:01,667 --> 00:11:03,002
Thanks to your assistance,

178
00:11:03,044 --> 00:11:06,590
I'm now fully aware
of what must be done.

179
00:11:06,631 --> 00:11:09,384
Though, sadly, I'm unable
to bring the girl back.

180
00:11:09,426 --> 00:11:12,262
I can promise you this:
The matter will be resolved

181
00:11:12,304 --> 00:11:14,598
in a way that I hope
brings you closure.

182
00:11:14,639 --> 00:11:16,682
[HOSTESS 05A]
You forgot something.

183
00:11:18,768 --> 00:11:20,228
[HOSTESS 05A]
In case you're curious,

184
00:11:20,270 --> 00:11:22,939
Frida's buried
in a potter's field.

185
00:11:22,981 --> 00:11:25,525
Unfortunately, even if the
girls and I pooled our earnings,

186
00:11:25,567 --> 00:11:28,987
we still couldn't afford
a proper headstone for her.

187
00:11:29,028 --> 00:11:32,365
Listen, mate. If you
feel any pity for the girl,

188
00:11:32,407 --> 00:11:36,328
use that money. Place some
flowers on her grave.

189
00:12:21,122 --> 00:12:23,625
[DUDLEY] You have the
package I entrusted to you?

190
00:12:23,667 --> 00:12:26,545
Yes, and as for the quality
of the newest shipment,

191
00:12:26,586 --> 00:12:29,297
it appears to be quite potent.

192
00:12:29,339 --> 00:12:32,258
He's resting comfortably inside.

193
00:12:40,266 --> 00:12:43,395
[DUDLEY] Are we feeling more
composed today, Lucian?

194
00:12:45,938 --> 00:12:48,816
[LUCIAN]
Frida?

195
00:12:48,858 --> 00:12:52,070
Unfortunately, the girl had a
slight accident and perished.

196
00:12:52,111 --> 00:12:54,030
Plunged right into the river.

197
00:12:54,072 --> 00:12:56,658
Wait, what? I don't understand.

198
00:12:56,700 --> 00:12:58,535
I made her a promise.

199
00:12:58,577 --> 00:13:01,079
[DUDLEY] I know you're having
difficulty processing this.

200
00:13:01,120 --> 00:13:02,706
I think it's best if you stay

201
00:13:02,747 --> 00:13:05,625
until your emotional
wounds are healed.

202
00:13:05,667 --> 00:13:09,128
Please, there's
no need to be hasty.

203
00:13:11,339 --> 00:13:13,550
[LUCIAN grunts]

204
00:13:16,761 --> 00:13:18,304
[WILLIAM]
Louis.

205
00:13:20,014 --> 00:13:23,226
I'd like you to send
those two a telegram for me.

206
00:13:23,268 --> 00:13:24,810
Then you mean...

207
00:13:26,229 --> 00:13:29,399
[WILLIAM] The time has come
for us to make our move.

208
00:13:54,591 --> 00:13:56,593
- -[knocking]
- -[MORAN groans]

209
00:13:56,635 --> 00:13:59,721
[FRED]
Excuse me, sir. A telegram.

210
00:14:09,439 --> 00:14:11,065
[MORAN chuckles]

211
00:14:24,120 --> 00:14:27,707
The brothers came all the way
down to the station to greet me.

212
00:14:27,749 --> 00:14:31,127
It's been far too long,
Colonel Moran.

213
00:14:31,169 --> 00:14:33,004
So we finally getting started?

214
00:14:33,045 --> 00:14:35,507
That's the reason you
sent me the telegram, innit?

215
00:14:35,548 --> 00:14:37,759
Now, now, all in good time.

216
00:14:37,801 --> 00:14:40,094
There's an order
to these things.

217
00:14:40,136 --> 00:14:44,766
On that note, I trust your
skills are as sharp as ever.

218
00:14:44,808 --> 00:14:47,852
You have to ask? Hm?

219
00:14:47,893 --> 00:14:50,313
If it isn't Fred!

220
00:14:50,355 --> 00:14:52,898
Haven't lost that
sunny disposition, I see.

221
00:14:52,940 --> 00:14:54,526
I requested that
he come before you

222
00:14:54,567 --> 00:14:56,068
to handle a certain errand.

223
00:14:56,110 --> 00:14:58,112
Did you locate what I asked for?

224
00:14:58,154 --> 00:15:00,281
[FRED]
Mm. I checked the hospital

225
00:15:00,323 --> 00:15:03,201
and found him in the
brothel two doors down.

226
00:15:03,242 --> 00:15:08,414
Thanks to the opium, he's not in
his right mind, least not yet.

227
00:15:08,456 --> 00:15:11,250
[WILLIAM] It appears the
stage is ready to be set.

228
00:15:12,293 --> 00:15:16,422
Now this job wasn't requested
by a client, but still...

229
00:15:27,099 --> 00:15:30,936
[WILLIAM] Gentlemen,
let's deliver some punishment.

230
00:15:37,485 --> 00:15:39,945
[MORAN]
Sadly, tonight's not your night.

231
00:15:39,987 --> 00:15:43,032
Wow! You're so good,
Mister Moran!

232
00:15:43,074 --> 00:15:46,494
What can I say, chaps? Looks
like I'm on a winning streak.

233
00:15:46,536 --> 00:15:47,620
No one's that lucky!

234
00:15:47,662 --> 00:15:50,248
Unless they've been
cheatin' this whole time!

235
00:15:53,125 --> 00:15:56,588
Fools all say the same thing
when they're down on their luck.

236
00:15:56,629 --> 00:16:01,133
And they were the blokes who
died first on the battlefield.

237
00:16:01,175 --> 00:16:03,469
So, Mister Moran, sir,

238
00:16:03,511 --> 00:16:05,680
now that you've made
all that money at cards,

239
00:16:05,722 --> 00:16:07,849
would you care to have
a different sort of fun?

240
00:16:07,891 --> 00:16:11,060
Sounds smashing. Your
room on the second floor?

241
00:16:11,102 --> 00:16:13,813
[BARMAID 05B] That's right. You
were quick to catch my meaning.

242
00:16:13,855 --> 00:16:15,398
[MORAN] And you were
quick to catch my eye

243
00:16:15,440 --> 00:16:16,691
when I stepped through the door.

244
00:16:16,733 --> 00:16:19,360
[BARMAID 05B]
Right this way, Romeo.

245
00:16:31,706 --> 00:16:33,708
[LUCIAN grunts]

246
00:16:35,919 --> 00:16:37,211
How'd I get here?

247
00:16:37,253 --> 00:16:39,255
[DUDLEY]
There you are, Lucian!

248
00:16:39,297 --> 00:16:42,842
[DUDLEY panting]

249
00:16:42,884 --> 00:16:45,970
Sir Dudley?

250
00:16:46,011 --> 00:16:48,431
Now wait. Let's discuss this.

251
00:16:48,473 --> 00:16:51,309
You could've asked us
to meet somewhere closer!

252
00:16:51,350 --> 00:16:53,185
What was the meaning
of that letter?!

253
00:16:53,227 --> 00:16:55,354
You're not actually going
to confess your crime!

254
00:16:55,396 --> 00:16:56,522
That's ludicrous!

255
00:16:56,564 --> 00:16:59,233
And after everything
I did to clean up after you!

256
00:16:59,275 --> 00:17:02,445
For that matter, how did you
even get out of your room?

257
00:17:02,487 --> 00:17:04,614
You cleaned up after me?

258
00:17:04,656 --> 00:17:06,115
[DUDLEY]
Of course!

259
00:17:06,157 --> 00:17:07,700
Why'd you have to
be so bloody careless

260
00:17:07,742 --> 00:17:10,244
and get that common
barmaid pregnant?

261
00:17:10,286 --> 00:17:14,540
Can you even imagine
the effort I went through?!

262
00:17:14,582 --> 00:17:17,752
[LUCIAN gasps]
Frida?

263
00:17:17,794 --> 00:17:19,921
[DUDLEY]
You are a nobleman!

264
00:17:19,963 --> 00:17:21,255
You shouldn't have
gotten involved

265
00:17:21,297 --> 00:17:24,383
with some backwater dishrag
like her in the first place!

266
00:17:24,425 --> 00:17:26,135
Surely you can see that!

267
00:17:26,177 --> 00:17:27,261
When the pen slips,

268
00:17:27,303 --> 00:17:29,305
you throw out the paper,
not the pen!

269
00:17:29,347 --> 00:17:32,266
It's the same way for people!
There's no changing it!

270
00:17:32,308 --> 00:17:35,186
That's the way the
aristocratic world operates!

271
00:17:35,227 --> 00:17:39,190
But I was supposed
to marry Frida.

272
00:17:39,231 --> 00:17:40,775
[DUDLEY]
That'll be quite enough of that!

273
00:17:40,817 --> 00:17:43,945
Now hold your tongue
and do exactly as I say!

274
00:17:43,987 --> 00:17:46,238
[FRIDA humming]

275
00:17:46,280 --> 00:17:48,240
[LUCIAN gasps]

276
00:17:51,828 --> 00:17:54,038
My love...

277
00:17:54,079 --> 00:17:56,374
[screams] It's impossible!

278
00:17:56,415 --> 00:17:58,334
You're dead!

279
00:17:58,376 --> 00:18:00,712
I killed you! I pumped
you full of opium,

280
00:18:00,753 --> 00:18:02,881
then you plunged to
your death in the river!

281
00:18:02,922 --> 00:18:04,298
What?

282
00:18:06,801 --> 00:18:09,888
At last, the truth from
the culprit's own mouth.

283
00:18:09,929 --> 00:18:13,933
The confession of
an unpardonable sin.

284
00:18:13,975 --> 00:18:17,186
[DUDLEY]
What? Professor Moriarty?

285
00:18:17,228 --> 00:18:19,480
Right, Fred. That'll do.

286
00:18:19,522 --> 00:18:21,148
Very well.

287
00:18:24,360 --> 00:18:26,111
You're a man.

288
00:18:26,153 --> 00:18:28,364
The fog is especially
heavy this evening.

289
00:18:28,406 --> 00:18:29,782
Combined with his slight build,

290
00:18:29,824 --> 00:18:31,993
he pulled off the illusion
spectacularly.

291
00:18:32,035 --> 00:18:33,369
Hold on,

292
00:18:33,411 --> 00:18:36,581
you wrote me that letter asking
to meet here, not Lucian!

293
00:18:36,622 --> 00:18:38,082
Guilty as charged.

294
00:18:38,123 --> 00:18:41,544
I'm the architect responsible
for designing this plot.

295
00:18:41,586 --> 00:18:43,671
But introductions are past due.

296
00:18:43,713 --> 00:18:47,967
I'm William James Moriarty,
Crime Consultant.

297
00:18:48,009 --> 00:18:50,011
[DUDLEY] What do you
mean "Crime Consultant"?

298
00:18:50,053 --> 00:18:51,888
And why are you
dressed like that?!

299
00:18:51,930 --> 00:18:55,307
[WILLIAM] Mister Bale,
I've done some research on you.

300
00:18:55,349 --> 00:18:57,393
In addition to working
for the university,

301
00:18:57,435 --> 00:18:59,938
you're also the owner
of several hospitals

302
00:18:59,979 --> 00:19:02,732
or should I say brothels?

303
00:19:02,774 --> 00:19:05,359
And is there a crime
against being a businessman?

304
00:19:05,401 --> 00:19:07,111
Is that what you're calling it?

305
00:19:07,152 --> 00:19:08,863
Your hospitals
served as a front,

306
00:19:08,905 --> 00:19:11,115
which allowed you to order
large quantities of opiates

307
00:19:11,156 --> 00:19:13,868
without arousing
anyone's suspicions.

308
00:19:13,910 --> 00:19:15,912
After you were fully supplied,

309
00:19:15,954 --> 00:19:19,874
you transformed the cellars of
your brothels into opium dens.

310
00:19:19,916 --> 00:19:23,127
You lure the sons of
aristocrats into vice and sin,

311
00:19:23,168 --> 00:19:25,755
then demand their parents
purchase your silence

312
00:19:25,797 --> 00:19:29,008
unless they want those deeds to
become public knowledge.

313
00:19:29,050 --> 00:19:31,886
Like a fire brigade that
goes around creating blazes,

314
00:19:31,928 --> 00:19:33,554
then offering your services.

315
00:19:33,596 --> 00:19:36,099
You are a different
class of despicable.

316
00:19:36,140 --> 00:19:38,726
Hah! You have all
the answers, don't you?

317
00:19:38,768 --> 00:19:40,853
Then go ahead and
turn me over to the police

318
00:19:40,895 --> 00:19:42,187
and see what happens.

319
00:19:42,229 --> 00:19:44,231
[WILLIAM]
I have no intention of that.

320
00:19:44,273 --> 00:19:45,524
Your claim of having influence

321
00:19:45,566 --> 00:19:48,486
with the local authorities
was not entirely unfounded.

322
00:19:48,527 --> 00:19:51,363
So then what are
you going to do?

323
00:19:51,405 --> 00:19:53,032
[WILLIAM]
I won't do anything.

324
00:19:53,074 --> 00:19:56,869
But you, overcome with the guilt
of Miss Macaulay's death,

325
00:19:56,911 --> 00:19:58,871
will dance yourself
into a frenzy

326
00:19:58,913 --> 00:20:00,915
before taking your own life.

327
00:20:00,957 --> 00:20:03,292
What?! Me, take my own life?!

328
00:20:03,334 --> 00:20:05,086
You're a bit
touched in the head.

329
00:20:05,128 --> 00:20:06,838
Why would I ever?

330
00:20:06,879 --> 00:20:08,798
[DUDLEY squeaks]

331
00:20:08,840 --> 00:20:10,883
Huh?! What the--?!

332
00:20:13,302 --> 00:20:14,637
[MORAN chuckles]

333
00:20:16,305 --> 00:20:20,977
[DUDLEY yelping]

334
00:20:21,019 --> 00:20:22,937
You've got quite
the lively step there.

335
00:20:22,979 --> 00:20:24,563
I've no doubt you'll prove to be

336
00:20:24,605 --> 00:20:26,983
an adequate match for
your dance partner.

337
00:20:27,025 --> 00:20:27,817
[shrieks]

338
00:20:27,859 --> 00:20:31,403
[DUDLEY panting]

339
00:20:33,489 --> 00:20:36,159
[WILLIAM] I don't think
you need any introduction.

340
00:20:36,200 --> 00:20:39,411
Who are you?!
Stop! Get away from me!

341
00:20:39,453 --> 00:20:41,372
[yelps]

342
00:20:43,875 --> 00:20:45,626
[gasps]

343
00:20:49,672 --> 00:20:51,757
[gasps]

344
00:20:51,799 --> 00:20:55,678
[screams]

345
00:20:59,807 --> 00:21:03,102
[LUCIAN cries]

346
00:21:23,998 --> 00:21:25,416
[MORAN]
Good on him.

347
00:21:25,457 --> 00:21:28,044
The kid erected
a fine tombstone.

348
00:21:28,086 --> 00:21:30,671
A love deemed impossible
because of class.

349
00:21:30,713 --> 00:21:34,092
Yeah. In a word, tragedy.

350
00:21:34,133 --> 00:21:35,801
Both Frida and he were victims

351
00:21:35,843 --> 00:21:38,262
of the country's
societal structure.

352
00:21:38,303 --> 00:21:39,680
But in a different world,

353
00:21:39,722 --> 00:21:43,308
the two of them would
have found happiness.

354
00:21:43,350 --> 00:21:45,561
A tragedy, indeed...

355
00:21:47,312 --> 00:21:49,607
[WILLIAM]
...and avoidable.

356
00:21:49,648 --> 00:21:52,777
Which is why we must
dismantle the system.

357
00:23:34,086 --> 00:23:37,089
[MORAN] Next time
on Moriarty the Patriot  .

358
00:23:37,131 --> 00:23:39,217
"The NOAHTIC Act 1."
